`),sampleAnswer:["Sportyz Goodz Ltd needs a coordinated financial and marketing response because the business is growing internationally while facing weaker sales and profitability. Expansion alone will not improve performance if the business does not manage its finances and marketing carefully.","One strategic role of financial management is to plan for the long-term financial needs of the business so shareholder wealth can be increased. This includes making decisions about funding, resource allocation, and risk so the business can remain competitive and financially sustainable.","Two suitable financial strategies are cash flow management and profitability management. Cash flow management is important because international expansion can create delays between spending and receiving revenue. Better cash budgeting, receivables control, and monitoring of outflows would help the business remain liquid. Profitability management is also needed because weaker sales and stronger competition suggest that costs, pricing, or product performance may need review.","Monitoring and controlling marketing is important because managers need to compare actual results with planned objectives. If market share, sales growth, or promotional outcomes are below target, the business can identify where the strategy is failing. This may lead to changes in promotion, product positioning, price, or target market selection.","Overall, the business should use financial management to support long-term growth while also checking that its marketing strategies are delivering results in a more competitive market."].join(`
`),marks:20})}},bre=["BS-HR-2"],xre=["human resource strategies and employment relations","marketing strategies and the marketing process"],wre={id:"business_studies/2017/q26",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...bre],learningTopics:xre,generate(){return Ee({question:"Analyse the response of human resource management to economic, technological and social influences.",sampleAnswer:["Human resource management must respond to outside influences because labour is not managed in isolation from the wider business environment. Economic, technological, and social changes all affect what employees need and what employers must do.","Economic influences such as recessions, inflation, or labour shortages affect staffing levels, wage decisions, and the use of part-time or casual employment. When economic conditions weaken, businesses may try to control costs through restructuring or downsizing. When conditions improve, they may focus more on recruitment and retention.","Technological influences change the skills employees need and the way work is organised. Human resource managers may need to provide retraining, introduce new communication systems, redesign jobs, or manage resistance to change when new technology is adopted.","Social influences include changing workforce participation, expectations about work-life balance, and growing acceptance of flexible work. In response, human resource management may introduce family-friendly policies, equal employment opportunity practices, and more flexible working arrangements.","These responses show that human resource management is shaped by broader influences. Effective managers do not just react to change; they adjust staffing, training, and workplace practices so the business can remain productive and legally compliant."].join(`
`),marks:20})}},vre=["BS-OP-2"],kre=["operations strategies and performance objectives","human resource strategies and employment relations","marketing strategies and the marketing process","financial objectives, ratios, and financial strategies"],Tre={id:"business_studies/2017/q27",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...vre],learningTopics:kre,generate(){return Ee({question:"Analyse the effect of globalisation on operations management.",sampleAnswer:["Globalisation has a major effect on operations management because it changes where businesses can source inputs, where they can produce, and who they compete against. Operations decisions are therefore no longer limited to local suppliers or local markets.","One effect is greater access to global sourcing. This can reduce costs and widen the choice of suppliers, but it can also increase transport delays, quality uncertainty, and ethical concerns. Operations managers must therefore balance lower prices against reliability and quality.","Globalisation also increases competitive pressure. Businesses may respond by improving efficiency, adopting better technology, or using economies of scale so they can match international competitors on price and quality.","Another effect is the spread of ideas and production methods across countries. Through scanning and learning, businesses can copy or adapt better systems used overseas. This can improve processes, but it may also require investment and staff retraining.","Overall, globalisation affects operations management significantly because it creates both opportunities and risks. The strongest operations responses are those that use global opportunities without losing control over quality, cost, and dependability."].join(`
