`),sampleAnswer:["Roo's Outback Eatery Pty Ltd is expanding by opening another restaurant, so it needs to protect the exclusive dining experience that customers already expect while also managing the extra financial pressure of growth.","To acquire staff effectively, the business should use recruitment and selection methods that identify employees with both technical ability and strong customer-service skills. Because the restaurant offers a modern Australian dining experience, it needs staff who can maintain quality, presentation, and service consistency. Interviews, reference checks, and practical work trials would help choose suitable applicants.","Staff development is also important. Training can build food knowledge, service standards, and teamwork, while performance management can monitor whether those standards are being met. Development should not only fix problems; it should help staff improve so that the customer experience remains consistent across both locations.","Two suitable working capital management strategies are cash flow management and inventory management. Cash flow management is necessary because opening a new restaurant can create high short-term costs before revenue becomes stable. Inventory management is also important because restaurants deal with perishable stock, so over-ordering can quickly create waste and reduce profitability.","Overall, the business should manage people and working capital together. Skilled, well-developed staff will help protect the premium dining experience, while strong control of cash and stock will support expansion without weakening financial performance."].join(`
`),marks:20})}},khe=["BS-MK-4"],The=["operations strategies and performance objectives","marketing strategies and the marketing process"],Ahe={id:"business_studies/2019/q26",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...khe],learningTopics:The,generate(){return Ee({question:"Analyse the relationship between market segmentation and marketing strategies.",sampleAnswer:["Market segmentation and marketing strategies are closely related because a business cannot design an effective marketing mix without first deciding which group of customers it wants to serve.","Segmentation divides the market into groups with similar characteristics such as age, income, lifestyle, location, or buying behaviour. Once the business identifies its segment, it can tailor product features, price, promotion, and distribution to suit that group.","For example, a business targeting a premium segment may use high-quality packaging, prestige pricing, and selective distribution. A business targeting price-sensitive consumers may choose simpler products, lower prices, and mass promotion. This shows that segmentation decisions directly shape strategy.","The relationship also works in reverse. A business may change its segmentation approach when current marketing strategies are not effective. If sales are weak, it may reposition the product for a different segment or redesign the marketing mix to better match customer needs.","Therefore, segmentation is not just a background step in marketing. It is a key influence on strategy because it determines who the business is trying to persuade and how the marketing mix should be designed."].join(`
`),marks:20})}},She=["BS-OP-5"],Che=["operations strategies and performance objectives","human resource strategies and employment relations","financial objectives, ratios, and financial strategies"],Ihe={id:"business_studies/2019/q27",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...She],learningTopics:Che,generate(){return Ee({question:"Analyse the relationship between performance objectives and operations strategies.",sampleAnswer:["Performance objectives and operations strategies are linked because objectives describe what the business wants to achieve, while strategies describe how operations management will achieve it.","For example, if a business wants to improve quality, it may use quality management systems, better technology, or improved training. If the objective is lower cost, it may consider outsourcing, leaner inventory systems, or economies of scale. If speed or dependability matters most, supply chain management and process layout become especially important.","This means operations strategies are not chosen randomly. They are selected because they help the business meet a particular performance objective. A strategy that works well for one objective may be less suitable for another. For instance, customisation may improve flexibility but raise costs.","The relationship is therefore one of alignment. When operations strategies match the most important performance objectives, the business is more likely to satisfy customers and remain competitive. When they do not match, operations may become inefficient or fail to deliver what the market expects.","Overall, performance objectives give direction to operations management, and operations strategies turn those objectives into practical action."].join(`
