`),sampleAnswer:["Bee Sticky Pty Ltd is expanding into Malaysia and the USA, so it needs marketing and finance strategies that protect its premium organic image while also managing the added risk of global operations.","Branding and product strategies should reinforce the business as a premium Australian organic honey producer. The branding should remain consistent so overseas customers recognise quality and authenticity, while product strategies may include adapting packaging, labels, or sizes to suit local market requirements. The key is to adapt the product without losing the premium position.","A suitable channel choice is selective distribution through carefully chosen retailers or specialist distributors. This gives the business access to overseas customers while helping protect brand image and maintain more control than a mass-distribution approach. The channel should match the premium market position rather than simply maximising outlet numbers.","Global financial management is necessary because expansion creates extra risk. The business must consider exchange rate movement, international payment methods, borrowing costs, and hedging strategies. If these risks are not managed well, global sales growth may not translate into stronger financial performance.","Overall, successful expansion requires coordinated branding, channel, and financial decisions. The business should pursue overseas growth in a way that preserves its premium image and limits unnecessary global financial risk."].join(`
