`),marks:20})}},afe=["BS-OP-4","BS-OP-5"],sfe=["operations strategies and performance objectives","marketing strategies and the marketing process","financial objectives, ratios, and financial strategies"],rfe={id:"business_studies/2022/q27",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...afe],learningTopics:sfe,generate(){return Ee({question:"Explain the importance to a business of having operations processes that can maintain a competitive advantage.",sampleAnswer:["Operations processes are important because they determine how consistently and efficiently the business can deliver value to customers. If those processes are strong, the business is more likely to keep a competitive advantage over time.","Effective operations processes improve quality, speed, dependability, and cost control. For example, better process design or technology can lower production costs, while strong quality control can reduce defects and strengthen customer trust.","These processes also matter because competitive advantage must be maintained, not just achieved once. A business may gain an advantage through innovation or good service, but it can lose that advantage if operations become inefficient or inconsistent.","Well-managed inputs, transformation, and outputs therefore support either cost leadership or differentiation. Poorly managed processes make it easier for competitors to overtake the business.","Overall, operations processes are important because they turn strategy into everyday performance. Without strong processes, competitive advantage is difficult to sustain."].join(`
