`),sampleAnswer:["Future Century Gaming Pty Ltd wants to expand globally, but skill shortages in Australia and the need for external finance mean that human resources and finance decisions are central to the success of that expansion.","The business may face recruiting and retaining challenges because skilled gaming and technology workers are scarce and often expensive. If labour supply is limited locally, the business may need to search international labour markets, but this can create extra costs, competition for talent, and integration challenges. Retention is also important because losing specialist employees can delay growth and increase recruitment costs.","Debt and equity finance each offer advantages and disadvantages. Debt finance allows the owners to keep control, but it increases repayment obligations and financial risk. Equity finance reduces the pressure of fixed repayments, but it dilutes ownership and may reduce control over future decisions.","A suitable recommendation would depend on the business context, but equity finance may be more appropriate if global expansion will take time to generate returns and the business wants to avoid heavy repayment pressure. Debt may still be suitable if cash flow is strong and control is a major priority.","Overall, the business should match its finance choice to its growth risk and cash-flow capacity while also ensuring it has the workforce needed to support global expansion."].join(`
`),marks:20})}},Lge=["BS-MK-2"],Pge=["operations strategies and performance objectives","marketing strategies and the marketing process","financial objectives, ratios, and financial strategies"],Ege={id:"business_studies/2023/q26",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...Lge],learningTopics:Pge,generate(){return Ee({question:"To what extent do influences on marketing affect business success?",sampleAnswer:["Influences on marketing affect business success to a large extent because marketing decisions only work when they match the environment in which the business is operating.","Psychological influences affect what customers value and how they respond to brands, pricing, and promotion. Sociocultural influences matter because changing lifestyles, values, and demographics can make one marketing approach effective and another outdated. Economic influences affect consumer spending power, while government influences shape what the business is legally allowed to promote and sell.","These influences matter because they affect the success of the marketing mix. A business that ignores them may choose the wrong target market, the wrong promotional message, or the wrong price. That can lead to weak sales and lost market share.","However, they do not determine success on their own. A business still needs strong products, operations, finance, and management. Marketing influences are therefore very important, but their effect depends on how well the business responds to them.","Overall, marketing influences affect business success to a significant extent because they shape the suitability of marketing strategies, but success still depends on the quality of the business response."].join(`
`),marks:20})}},Oge=["BS-OP-2"],Nge=["operations strategies and performance objectives","human resource strategies and employment relations","marketing strategies and the marketing process","financial objectives, ratios, and financial strategies"],Mge={id:"business_studies/2023/q27",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...Oge],learningTopics:Nge,generate(){return Ee({question:"To what extent do influences on operations affect business success?",sampleAnswer:["Influences on operations affect business success to a large extent because operations is where the business turns resources into products or services for customers.","Globalisation, technology, quality expectations, legal regulation, and environmental sustainability all affect how operations must be managed. They can change costs, efficiency, compliance obligations, and customer expectations. If operations management responds well, the business may improve quality, reduce waste, and stay competitive.","The effect is significant because many business outcomes depend on operations performance. A business with weak operations may face delays, poor quality, higher costs, or legal problems, all of which can damage sales and reputation.","However, operations influences are not the only factor affecting success. Marketing, finance, and human resources also matter. This means operations influences are highly important, but their overall effect depends on how the whole business responds.","Overall, these influences affect business success to a considerable extent because they shape day-to-day performance, but success still depends on coordinated management across all business functions."].join(`
