`),sampleAnswer:["Hans-Made Watches is trying to improve performance in a market where sales and market share are falling. Because it sells handmade European-style watches with a lifetime warranty, the business already has a product position that can support a premium strategy, but its people management is weakening that advantage.","The business uses product differentiation by offering handmade quality, distinctive style, and a lifetime warranty. These features set the watches apart from cheaper mass-produced alternatives and give customers a reason to value the product for more than price alone.","The current acquisition process is weak because it relies on family and friends and does not require experience. This limits the pool of applicants and increases the risk of hiring people who do not have the skills needed to improve production, customer service, or business performance.","Appropriate human resource strategies include stronger recruitment and selection, training and development, and performance management. A wider recruitment process would attract more suitable candidates. Training can improve technical and customer-service skills. Performance management would help ensure employees meet standards linked to quality and sales outcomes.","Overall, the business already has a differentiated product, but better human resource strategies are needed if that product advantage is to translate into stronger sales and market share."].join(`
