`),sampleAnswer:["**Factor 1 — Use of a catalyst:**","","Catalysts are used in both reactors (Reactor 1 and Reactor 2). A catalyst increases the rate of reaction at a lower temperature, making the process more energy-efficient and economically viable.","","**Factor 2 — Recycling of unreacted reagents:**","","After Separator 1, unreacted ethene and oxygen are recycled back to Reactor 1. This maximises the use of raw materials, reduces waste, and improves the atom economy and profitability of the process.","","**Factor 3 — Access to markets:**","","The major product (ethane-1,2-diol) and the by-products are both transported to markets for sale. By ensuring all outputs have commercial value (near 100% atom economy), the process is made economically sustainable. The plant location would be chosen near transport networks to facilitate efficient product delivery."].join(`
