`),sampleAnswer:["**Enthalpy and entropy of the forward reaction ($\\mathrm{H_2O(l) \\rightarrow H_2O(g)}$):**","","- $\\Delta H > 0$ (endothermic — energy is required to break intermolecular forces).","- $\\Delta S > 0$ (entropy increases as liquid becomes gas with greater disorder).","","At $23\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}$ (below the boiling point), $\\Delta H > T\\Delta S$, so $\\Delta G > 0$.","The forward reaction is **non-spontaneous** under standard conditions.","","**Water in the open beaker:**","","The beaker is open to the atmosphere, so water vapour produced diffuses away.","The concentration of $\\mathrm{H_2O(g)}$ above the surface remains low: $Q < K_{eq}$.","Because $Q$ remains less than $K_{eq}$, the forward reaction is continuously favoured,","and the water **continuously evaporates** (a net loss of water is observed).","","**Water in the sealed bottle:**","","The bottle is closed, so $\\mathrm{H_2O(g)}$ accumulates above the liquid surface.","Eventually $[\\mathrm{H_2O(g)}]$ rises until $Q = K_{eq}$ and **dynamic equilibrium is established**.","At equilibrium, the rate of evaporation equals the rate of condensation;","the water level in the bottle appears unchanged."].join(`
