`),sampleAnswer:["The **DMC process** is preferable.","","**Higher atom economy:** The DMC process has AE = 48.4% compared to 35.9% for the phosgene process.","A higher atom economy means a greater fraction of the atoms from the reactants end up in the desired urea product rather than in by-products. This means the DMC process wastes less material per mole of urea produced.","","**Safer reagents:** The question states that phosgene has **high toxicity**, whereas DMC has **low toxicity**.","Using the less toxic starting material is preferable because it reduces risk during storage, transport, handling and large-scale processing. This improves worker safety and lowers the chance of serious environmental harm if there is an accidental release.","","**Overall judgement:** Green chemistry favours processes that reduce waste and reduce hazard. Since the DMC route is both safer and more atom-economical, it is the better process based on the information provided."].join(`
