`),sampleAnswer:["The energy profile shows that the forward reaction is exothermic.","By Le Chatelier's principle, cooling removes heat, so the system responds by favouring the exothermic forward reaction. This produces more $\\mathrm{Co(H_2O)_6^{2+}}$, which is pink.","Collision theory explains that lowering the temperature reduces the average kinetic energy of particles, so both forward and reverse reactions slow down.","However, the reverse reaction slows down more because it has the larger activation energy. A larger fraction of particles now fall below $E_{a2}$ than below $E_{a1}$.","Therefore the forward reaction becomes relatively more successful than the reverse reaction, so the concentration of the pink complex increases and the solution turns pink."].join(`
