`),choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["In a collaborative design approach, team members work together to discuss and share ideas.","","Collaborative design is defined by active participation and open communication among","team members. Ideas, feedback, and expertise are shared freely across the group,","leading to more creative and well-rounded outcomes.","","Multi-tasking describes individual workload management, not collaboration.","A project manager directing ideas describes a hierarchical, not collaborative, structure.","Allocating a single project to all team members describes resource allocation,","not the nature of collaboration itself."].join(`
