`),choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["Companies incorporate built-in obsolescence to increase the probability of consistent sales.","","Built-in obsolescence is the practice of intentionally designing a product to have","a limited lifespan or to become outdated. When a product stops functioning or is","superseded by a newer model, consumers need to purchase a replacement, generating","repeat sales for the manufacturer.","","Sustainability and product longevity are not goals of built-in obsolescence —","in fact, planned obsolescence works against these outcomes.","Making products safer or longer-lasting would reduce the frequency of repeat purchases,","which is the opposite of the commercial motivation."].join(`
`)}}}},Uqe=["DT-DP-4"],Vqe=["sustainable design and environmental impact","life cycle analysis, waste reduction, and product longevity"],Xqe={id:"design_and_technology/2016/q10",version:1,variants:4,syllabusTopics:[...Uqe],learningTopics:Vqe,generate(t){const e=[3,0,1,2][t],n="Provide the consumer with products that are environmentally friendly and use the minimum amount of resources",i=["Create designs that follow the latest trends","Ensure that a product will be durable and competitive in the marketplace","Seek to reduce both the negative impact of the design on the environment and the cost to the consumer"],o=[];let a=0;for(let s=0;s<4;s++)o.push(s===e?n:i[a++]);return{question:"How can designers best achieve sustainable design?",choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["Designers best achieve sustainable design by providing consumers with products that","are environmentally friendly and use the minimum amount of resources.","","Sustainable design aims to meet present needs without compromising future generations.","This is best achieved by minimising resource consumption throughout the product's","entire life cycle — from raw material extraction through manufacture, use, and disposal.","Environmentally friendly products reduce pollution, waste, and depletion of finite resources.","","Following trends prioritises commercial appeal over sustainability.","Durability and competitiveness are related but incomplete as a sustainability definition.","Reducing cost to the consumer is a commercial goal, not a sustainability principle."].join(`
