`),choices:i,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:n,explanation:["A designer would first create a CAD model at the presentation of ideas for feedback stage.","","CAD (Computer-Aided Design) models are used to present developed design concepts","to clients and stakeholders in a clear, three-dimensional format. This allows for","meaningful feedback before committing to detailed development or production.","","During initial client contact, ideas are still being gathered. During brainstorming,","concepts are sketched informally. CAD modelling requires a sufficiently developed","concept and is therefore used at the presentation stage, not at the earliest stages.","Reflection and changes come after the initial CAD presentation."].join(`
