`)},{group:"people with physical disabilities",correctPos:0,correct:"Able to meet a need and be ergonomically designed",distractors:["Durable and well made","Cost effective and easy to store","Aesthetically pleasing and easy to use"],explanation:["When designing an aid for people with physical disabilities, the designer would","first consider that the end product is able to meet a need and be ergonomically designed.","","The primary purpose of an assistive aid is to address a specific functional need.","Ergonomic design ensures the product can be used comfortably and effectively by","people with varying physical abilities, reducing strain and supporting independence.","","Durability, cost, and aesthetics are secondary considerations when the core goal","is functional accessibility."].join(`
