`),correctPos:2,question:"Which of the following is a direct benefit of this trend to the consumer?",choices:["Increased sales","Greater privacy","Greater convenience","A greener environment"],explanation:["Greater convenience is the direct benefit to consumers from a cashless and","paperless society. Consumers can pay quickly and easily using transport cards","or contactless payments without needing to carry cash or paper tickets,","saving time and effort.","","Option A (Increased sales) is a benefit to businesses and retailers, not","directly to consumers.","","Option B (Greater privacy) is not a direct benefit — digital payment systems","often involve more data collection and tracking than cash transactions,","which can reduce privacy rather than increase it.","","Option D (A greener environment) may be an indirect or partial benefit,","but it is not the most direct benefit experienced by individual consumers.","The primary experience for the consumer is the ease and speed of","making payments and accessing services."].join(`
