`),correctPos:0,question:"Which of the following is a direct benefit of this trend to the consumer?",choices:["Increased revenue for retailers","Greater ownership of content","Greater convenience","Reduced screen time"],explanation:["Greater convenience is the primary direct benefit to consumers from the rise","of video streaming services. Consumers can instantly access a vast library of","content from any device at any time, without needing to purchase, store, or","return physical media.","","Option A (Increased revenue for retailers) is a benefit to streaming","companies and businesses, not to individual consumers.","","Option B (Greater ownership of content) is actually the opposite of what","streaming provides — consumers typically licence content rather than own it,","so ownership is reduced compared to buying physical media.","","Option D (Reduced screen time) is not a consequence of streaming growth;","in fact, the availability of on-demand content tends to increase screen time."].join(`
