`),choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["The ethical responsibility of a designer when using synthetic materials is","to inform consumers of the materials used in the product. Consumers have a","right to know what a product is made from — this supports informed","decision-making, especially for those with health concerns, ethical","purchasing preferences, or environmental values.","","Option A (Develop a returns policy) is a commercial consideration, not an","ethical one specific to the use of synthetic materials. A returns policy","does not address the consumer's right to know what a product contains.","","Option C (Promote the lack of environmental damage) is potentially","misleading. Synthetic materials can have significant environmental impacts","during production and disposal, and promoting claims of no environmental","damage without evidence would be unethical.","","Option D (Assure consumers that composition and appearance are the same)","is factually incorrect. Natural and synthetic materials differ in chemical","composition and often in appearance, texture, and performance. Making","false assurances to consumers is unethical."].join(`
