`),choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["The primary purpose of a WHS risk assessment is to identify and assess","potential injury or illness in the workplace.","","A risk assessment is a systematic process of examining work activities","and environments to identify hazards that could cause harm, evaluating","the likelihood and severity of potential injury or illness, and then","putting controls in place to minimise that risk.","","Identifying dangerous equipment is only one part of a broader risk","assessment. Evaluating workshop organisation and assessing environmental","impact of materials are related but more narrow or distinct purposes."].join(`
`)}}}},ZOe=["DT-DP-3","DT-DP-4"],eNe=["sustainable design and environmental impact","life cycle analysis, waste reduction, and product longevity"],tNe={id:"design_and_technology/2023/q06",version:1,variants:4,syllabusTopics:[...ZOe],learningTopics:eNe,generate(t){const e=[2,3,0,1][t],n="it cannot be repaired because parts are not available.",i=["it is ageing.","it is classified as an antique.","a variety of materials is considered during design and development."],o=[];let a=0;for(let s=0;s<4;s++)o.push(s===e?n:i[a++]);return{question:"A product is obsolescent when",choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["A product is obsolescent when it cannot be repaired because parts are not","available.","","Obsolescence refers to the process of a product becoming outdated or no","longer functional. A key form of planned or natural obsolescence occurs","when spare parts are discontinued, making it impossible to repair the","product and forcing consumers to replace it.","","Simply being old or ageing does not make a product obsolescent — antiques","are old yet still valued. The variety of materials considered during","design is unrelated to obsolescence."].join(`
