`)}}}},ONe=["DT-DP-4"],NNe=["sustainable design and environmental impact","life cycle analysis, waste reduction, and product longevity"],MNe={id:"design_and_technology/2024/q02",version:1,variants:4,syllabusTopics:[...ONe],learningTopics:NNe,generate(t){const e=[2,3,0,1][t],n="To ensure the long-term availability of natural resources",i=["To preserve the ozone layer","To reduce pollution and waste","To promote the responsible use of affordable materials by manufacturers"],o=[];let a=0;for(let s=0;s<4;s++)o.push(s===e?n:i[a++]);return{question:"What is the main goal of sustainable design?",choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["The main goal of sustainable design is to ensure the long-term availability","of natural resources.","","Sustainable design considers the environmental impact of products across their","entire lifecycle — from sourcing materials through to disposal. Its core aim is","to meet present needs without compromising the ability of future generations to","meet their own needs, which fundamentally depends on the continued availability","of natural resources.","","Reducing pollution and preserving the ozone layer are related environmental","benefits, but they are outcomes of sustainable practice rather than its primary","goal. Promoting affordable materials focuses on economics rather than sustainability."].join(`
