`),choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["The designer should initially research existing images and symbols.","","When responding to a design brief, the first step is to research visual and","conceptual content that is relevant to the design task. For greeting cards,","this means understanding the range of images, symbols, motifs, and themes","already used in the market, which provides a foundation for generating","original design ideas.","","Supply strategies, timelines, and product development actions are important","later in the design process, but they are not the initial research focus.","Gift card values are unrelated to developing new greeting card designs."].join(`
`)}}}},RNe=["DT-DP-3","DT-DP-4"],FNe=["client needs analysis and target market research","user-centred design decision-making","ethical and legal responsibilities in design","privacy, security, and responsible decision-making"],DNe={id:"design_and_technology/2024/q04",version:1,variants:4,syllabusTopics:[...RNe],learningTopics:FNe,generate(t){const e=[3,0,1,2][t],n="End user wellbeing and environmental friendliness",i=["Social trends and convenience","Financial market share and existing products","Patent protection and niche market compatibility"],o=[];let a=0;for(let s=0;s<4;s++)o.push(s===e?n:i[a++]);return{question:"What are the prime considerations for designers when producing safe and ethical products for consumers?",choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["The prime considerations for designers producing safe and ethical products are","end user wellbeing and environmental friendliness.","","Safe and ethical design requires that the needs and safety of the end user are","placed at the centre of all design decisions. This means considering health risks,","ergonomic factors, and the overall impact on the people who will use the product.","Environmental friendliness reflects the ethical responsibility of designers to","minimise harm to the natural world through material choices, production processes,","and end-of-life disposal.","","While social trends, financial considerations, and patent protection are relevant","business concerns, they are not the primary ethical considerations guiding safe","product design."].join(`
`)}}}},zNe=["DT-DP-5"],YNe=["design process decision-making","evaluating design solutions against a brief"],WNe={id:"design_and_technology/2024/q05",version:1,variants:4,syllabusTopics:[...zNe],learningTopics:YNe,generate(t){const e=[3,0,1,2][t],n="Shared understanding of the project, various fields of professional expertise, cooperative decision-making process",i=["Leader directed, common skills among the group, responsive to feedback","Leader directed, various fields of professional expertise, responsive to feedback","Shared understanding of the project, common skills among the team, cooperative decision-making process"],o=[];let a=0;for(let s=0;s<4;s++)o.push(s===e?n:i[a++]);return{question:"Which of the following options best describes the features of a collaborative design team?",choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["A collaborative design team is best described as having a shared understanding","of the project, various fields of professional expertise, and a cooperative","decision-making process.","","Collaboration means all team members work together toward a common goal with","a shared understanding of the project brief and objectives. Effective design teams","bring together specialists from different disciplines (e.g. industrial designers,","engineers, marketers, and user experience experts) rather than people with the same","skills. Decisions are reached cooperatively through discussion and consensus,","rather than being directed by a single leader.","","Leader-directed teams with common skills describe a hierarchical or siloed model,","which is not the defining feature of collaboration."].join(`
