`)}}}},XNe=["DT-IET-1"],KNe=["intellectual property protection in design","matching patents, copyright, trademarks, and registered designs to a solution","ethical and legal responsibilities in design","privacy, security, and responsible decision-making"],QNe={id:"design_and_technology/2024/q07",version:1,variants:4,syllabusTopics:[...XNe],learningTopics:KNe,generate(t){const e=[1,2,3,0][t],n="The corporation applies for a patent.",i=["The designer applies for a patent.","The designer applies for copyright protection.","The corporation applies for copyright protection."],o=[];let a=0;for(let s=0;s<4;s++)o.push(s===e?n:i[a++]);return{question:["A corporation has commissioned a designer to develop a new solar-powered,","mobile interactive game.","","What is an ethical way to protect the intellectual property of the new design?"].join(`
`),choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["The corporation applies for a patent.","","When a designer is commissioned by a corporation, the intellectual property","of the resulting design typically belongs to the client (the corporation)","rather than the individual designer, unless a contract states otherwise.","Since the design is an invention — a novel solar-powered device — a patent","is the appropriate form of IP protection (patents cover inventions, not","just creative works).","","Copyright protection is generally used for creative works such as written,","artistic, or musical works, and is less suited to protect a functional","product design. Because the corporation owns the commissioned work,","the designer applying on their own behalf would not be ethical or legally","appropriate."].join(`
`)}}}},JNe=["DT-DP-4"],ZNe=["sustainable design and environmental impact","life cycle analysis, waste reduction, and product longevity","innovation and emerging technologies in design","social, ethical, and environmental impacts of innovation"],eMe={id:"design_and_technology/2024/q08",version:1,variants:4,syllabusTopics:[...JNe],learningTopics:ZNe,generate(t){const e=[2,3,0,1][t],n="To understand the impact of the project on society and the environment",i=["To establish the rights of the designer","To research the possibility of future growth in market share","To determine the level of consumer demand for the newly developed product"],o=[];let a=0;for(let s=0;s<4;s++)o.push(s===e?n:i[a++]);return{question:"What is the most important reason for undertaking a life cycle analysis of an innovative design?",choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["The most important reason for undertaking a life cycle analysis is to understand","the impact of the project on society and the environment.","","A life cycle analysis (LCA) examines every stage of a product's life — from","raw material extraction and manufacturing through to use and end-of-life disposal.","Its primary purpose is to identify and assess the social and environmental","consequences of the product across its entire lifespan, enabling designers","to make more sustainable and responsible decisions.","","Establishing designer rights is a legal matter handled separately through IP law.","Market share research and consumer demand assessment are commercial activities","relevant to marketing, not the core purpose of an LCA."].join(`
