`),choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:i,explanation:["A globular cluster forms when a large group of stars is created from the","same cloud of gas over a relatively short time on an astronomical scale.","So the stars in that cluster are taken to have formed at about the same time.","","That means the stars have approximately the same **age**.","","Their **colour** and **luminosity** can still be different because stars of","different masses sit at different positions on the Hertzsprung-Russell diagram.","Their **masses** are also not all the same, because stars in a cluster are","born with a range of initial masses.","","So the quantity that is approximately the same for stars in a globular","cluster is their **age**."].join(`
