`),choices:o,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:i,explanation:["A sinusoidal alternating voltage is produced when a **coil rotates at constant","speed in a magnetic field**. As the coil turns, the magnetic flux through it","changes smoothly, so the induced EMF changes smoothly as well.","","By Faraday's law, the induced EMF depends on the rate of change of flux:","","$$\\mathcal{E} = -\\dfrac{d\\Phi}{dt}$$","","For uniform rotation, this gives a **sine-wave AC output**.","","The device therefore needs two key features:","- a rotating coil between magnetic poles","- slip rings connecting the rotating coil to the external circuit","","Slip rings allow the current to reverse naturally every half-turn, so the","output remains alternating. A **split-ring commutator** would reverse the","connections every half-turn and produce **pulsating DC** instead.","","A **transformer** does not generate electricity at all. It only changes the","voltage of an existing AC supply."].join(`
