`),sampleAnswer:["**Qualitative explanation of time dilation:**","","In the **inside observer's frame** (on the train), the light pulse travels","straight up and down between the mirrors — a short path.","","In the **outside observer's frame** (stationary), the train is moving, so","the light pulse travels a longer diagonal path (like a zigzag) to keep up","with the moving mirrors.","","Einstein's postulate states that the **speed of light is the same** ($c$)","for all inertial observers. Since speed = distance/time and the outside","observer sees the light travel a **longer distance** at the same speed $c$,","the outside observer must measure a **longer time** for the same event.","","This means time passes **more slowly** in the moving frame — **time dilation**."].join(`
