`),sampleAnswer:["The statement is **incorrect**. While it is true that the larger current in","rod A contributes to the electromagnetic force between the rods, the statement","misidentifies the cause of rod B's larger displacement.","","**Newton's third law** states that the force rod A exerts on rod B is equal","in magnitude (but opposite in direction) to the force rod B exerts on rod A.","The magnitude of the electromagnetic force between the rods is given by:","$$\\frac{F}{L} = \\frac{\\mu_0 I_A I_B}{2\\pi r}$$","This depends on **both** currents; the same magnitude of force acts on each rod.","","Since the forces are equal in magnitude, the difference in displacement must","be due to the rods having **different masses**.","Rod B has a smaller mass, so by Newton's second law ($a = F/m$), rod B","experiences a greater acceleration and therefore reaches a larger displacement","in the same time $t$."].join(`
