`),WLn(),["When Earth was at position $P$, the orbital period of Io was measured,","and the time that Io was at position $R$ was recorded. Six months later,","Io had orbited Jupiter 103 times, and Earth had reached position $Q$.","The orbital period of Io was used to predict when it would be at position $R$.","Assume that Jupiter has not moved significantly in its orbit around the Sun.","","The time for Io to reach position $R$ was measured to be","$1.000 \\times 10^3$ s later than predicted, due to the time it takes light","to cross the diameter of Earth's orbit from $P$ to $Q$."].join(`
