`)],sampleAnswer:["**Why the balance reading increases**","","As the magnet falls inside the copper pipe, the magnetic flux through","sections of the copper pipe changes. By **Faraday's law**, this changing","flux induces an electromotive force (emf) and hence an induced current in","the copper pipe.","","By **Lenz's law**, the direction of the induced current is such that it","opposes the change in flux — i.e., it opposes the downward motion of the","magnet, producing an upward magnetic braking force on the magnet.","","By **Newton's third law**, if the magnet experiences an upward force from","the pipe, the pipe experiences an equal and opposite **downward** reaction","force from the magnet. This additional downward force is transmitted through","the pipe to the balance, causing the reading to increase above 300 g.","","**Why the reading reaches a constant maximum of 350 g**","","As the magnet accelerates, the rate of change of flux — and therefore the","magnitude of the braking force — increases. Eventually the upward magnetic","braking force equals the weight of the magnet ($mg$, equivalent to 50 g-force).","At this point the net force on the magnet is zero and it reaches **terminal","velocity** (constant speed).","","At terminal velocity, the braking force on the magnet = its weight (50 g-force).","The reaction on the pipe is therefore equal to the weight of the magnet.","The balance then reads:","","$$300\\text{ g} + 50\\text{ g} = 350\\text{ g}$$","","This equals the total weight of the system (pipe + magnet), which makes","physical sense: once the magnet moves at constant velocity the system as a","whole is in equilibrium, and the balance supports the full combined weight.","","The maximum is reached **before** the magnet hits the bottom, confirming","it reached terminal velocity within the pipe.","","So the two observations are linked: induction creates a magnetic braking force,","and once that braking force grows until it balances the magnet's weight, the","balance must read the full combined weight of the pipe and magnet."].join(`
